equired": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 39500, "description": "##Special 2hr Theater History Tours with BBF and the Boch Center Wang Theatre - \nJoin us on Sun Oct 6, Tue Oct 15 and Sun Oct 27, 2024 for a unique 2 hour Theater History program that includes both Boston By Foot's guided Theater District tour followed by a guided tour of the interior of the Historic Boch Center Wang Theatre & Folk Americana Roots Hall of Fame. BBF members receive a discount on 2hr Theater History tour tickets (Sun Oct 6 this tour will be offered free to BBF members as a member preview, join us as a BBF member to get early access to this program!) These special 2 hour Theater History tours are presented in collaboration with [The Boch Center Wang Theatre] (https://www.bochcenter.org). All are welcome. \n\n##About Boston By Foot's Theater District walking tour\nTake a walking tour of Boston's Theater District.  Join your Boston By Foot guide for walking tour of Boston's Theater District exploring the exteriors of such theatres as the Opera House, the Majestic, Wilbur, Colonial, and the Paramount.  Experience stories about the varied history of theatre in Boston, from the Colonial period to Boston's heyday as a tryout venue for some of the country's greatest plays and musicals before they went to Broadway.\n\n##About the Historic Boch Center Wang Theatre interior tour\nEnjoy a behind-the-scenes tour of one of Boston’s most prominent landmarks, the historic Boch Center Wang Theatre - plus get an exclusive look at the Folk Americana Roots Hall of Fame and its multiple exhibits! Learn about the theatre’s architectural highlights and unique history – from its hotel roots and glamorous days as a movie “cathedral”, to today’s role as an impressive venue for performances and events. Stand on the stage graced by Mikhail Baryshnikov, Queen, Elton John, Lady Gaga, Liza Minnelli and more! Explore The Music Hall and learn about the home of the first Folk Americana Roots Hall of Fame - featuring memorabilia and photographs of music legends such as Neil Young, Bruce Springsteen, Joan Baez, and Bob Dylan\n\n##Duration, Distance, Terrain \n- Special 2hr tour includes a 60-75 minute walking tour of Boston's Theater District followed by a 45-60min tour of the Boch Center Wang Theatre\n- Walking Tour terrain: mostly flat surfaces with little to no inclines\n\n##Meeting location:\nMeet your guide in front of the Citizens Bank Opera House, 539 Washington Street, Boston\n\nFinding Your Guide: All guides carry an 8×11 sign that says “Boston By Foot Walking Tours.”\n\nNearest MBTA Stations: Downtown Crossing (Red and Orange lines), or Chinatown (Orange line)\n\n##What to bring\nComfortable shoes, dress for the weather, water bottle", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "Experience the colorful history of theatre in Boston!", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/566969/images/1260538/", "pk": 1260538, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/pVq5sSdXRCS5blAEGiQh", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/pVq5sSdXRCS5blAEGiQh", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/"}, "item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/566969/"}, "crop": {}, "cropped_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/pVq5sSdXRCS5blAEGiQh", "cropped_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/pVq5sSdXRCS5blAEGiQh", "is_low_resolution": false, "has_text_overlay": true, "has_logo_overlay": false}, {"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/566969/images/1261003/", "pk": 1261003, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https